      "l": "MIDDLE OVERS",
      "c": "ink"
     },
     {
      "v": "+1.2",
      "l": "DEATH OVERS",
      "c": "muted"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "vo": "That's the first surprise. The death overs were always explosive. The real revolution happened at the start of the innings, and in the overs nobody used to care about.",
   "scene": {
    "type": "statement",
    "lines": [
     {
      "t": "THE REVOLUTION"
     },
     {
      "t": "HAPPENED"
     },
     {
      "t": "AT THE START.",
      "c": "gold"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "vo": "And it's a revolution of sixes. Fours per match barely moved for a decade: between twenty-six and twenty-eight a game, every season until twenty twenty-two. Sixes went from under nine a match in twenty thirteen, to nearly twenty in twenty twenty-six.",
