  },
  {
   "vo": "Here's the strike rate of the top three in the batting order, against the middle order, numbers four to seven. For ten years, they moved together. The top order was often the slower of the two, playing the anchor role. Then, from twenty twenty-three, the top three took off. One forty-three. Then one fifty-four, one fifty-nine, and one sixty-six in twenty twenty-six. The middle order stalled at around one fifty.",
